course: dictionary
lesson: 16122
title: A whiff of meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A whiff is a short, faint smell. You might get a whiff of bread as you walk past a bakery. When you meet the word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «She got a whiff of cooking as she came in from school.» Cooking makes a smell and dinner is near, so a whiff must be a small smell.
explain: The same word can also mean a slight sign of something. «The detective caught a whiff of a lie in the man's story.» Nobody can smell a lie! The word is used like a clue, a faint hint that something is there. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A hint fits better than a smell.
explain: Look at the word's job in the sentence. In «Your trainers whiff!» whiff is a verb, an action word, and it means they smell bad. In US baseball, a batter can whiff, which means they swing at the ball and miss it completely. The same spelling can mean different things in different places.
explain: In a safety lesson, a whiff of gas or smoke is a warning. «If you get a whiff of gas, tell an adult and get out.» Even a tiny smell matters, so never ignore it.
fact: A whiff is a short, faint smell.
fact: «A whiff of smoke» means a small sign that there may be a fire nearby.
fact: «A whiff of danger» means a slight hint that something dangerous could happen.
fact: In UK informal speech, whiff as a verb means to smell bad.
fact: In US sport, to whiff means to swing at a ball and miss it completely.
exercise: «The sweet whiff of cooking drifted down the hall.» What does whiff mean here? | *A short, faint smell | A long, heavy rain | A loud crash | A thick layer of paint
exercise: Dad laughs and says, «Your trainers whiff!» What does whiff mean? | To hide something | *To smell bad | To swing and miss | To shout loudly
exercise: «The hunter caught a whiff of danger in the air.» What does a whiff of danger suggest? | A big storm coming soon | *A slight sign that danger is near | A happy party with music | A long, sleepy afternoon
test: «If you get a whiff of gas, what should you do?» | Keep it a secret | Open a window and strike a match | *Tell an adult and get out | Go back to sleep
test: «In a baseball game, the batter whiffed on the third pitch.» What does whiffed mean? | *Swung and missed the ball completely | Ran to first base | Hit the ball over the fence | Caught the ball
exam: Which phrase means to notice a faint smell for a short time? | pour a cup of | *catch a whiff of | count the stars in | sing a song about
